            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            which assigns to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number"} number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(n)
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partitions"} partitions
            (into
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multisets"} multisets
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            = succeed "." do
              %em paritition function
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#generating_function Generating function
          %p
            Its (ordinary)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generating+function"} generating function
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi k
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sum_{n=0}^\infty p(n) x^n = \prod_{k=1}^\infty (1 - x^k)^{-1}
                  \\,.
          %h3#AsymptoticExpansion Asymptotic expansion
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+expansion"} asymptotic expansion
            of the partition function is (
            %a{:href => "#HardyRamanujan1918"}> Hardy &amp; Ramanujan 1918
            , see
            %a{:href => "#DeSalvo20"} DeSalvo 20
            for discussion)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∼
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mrow
                          %msqrt
                            %mrow
                              %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mn 3
                          %mi π
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msqrt
                            %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                      %msqrt
                        %mn 3
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  p(n)
                  \\;\sim\;
                  \\frac
                  { e^{ \sqrt{2/3}\pi \cdot \sqrt{n} } }
                  { 4 \sqrt{3} \cdot n}
                  \\,.
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              On-Line Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://oeis.org/A000041"} OEIS A000041
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Partition_function_(number_theory)"} Partition function (number theory)
          %p Asymptotic behaviour:
          %ul
            %li#HardyRamanujan1918
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Godfrey+Hardy"}> Godfrey Hardy
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Srinivasa+Ramanujan"} Srinivasa Ramanujan
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Asymptotic formulaæ in combinatory analysis
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/plms/s2-17.1.75"} doi:10.1112/plms/s2-17.1.75
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HardyRamanujanAsymptoticFormulae.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#DeSalvo20
              %p
                Stephen DeSalvo,
                %em Will the real Hardy-Ramanujan formula please stand up?
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.06908"}> arXiv:2003.06908
                )
